course: dictionary
lesson: 9640
title: Stupid, and why some words hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word stupid means not clever or not sensible, as in «a stupid mistake». It can also describe something silly or annoying, as in «this stupid zip won't work». Use the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Be careful with stupid when you talk about a person. Calling someone stupid is rude and hurts feelings, so teachers usually prefer words like silly, careless or not a good idea. «Don't be stupid» is a warning, not a compliment.
explain: In a safety talk, «doing something stupid» means taking a dangerous risk, such as a dare. In a story, stupid often shows anger or frustration. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Stupid is an adjective: stupid, stupider or more stupid, stupidest or most stupid.
fact: «A stupid mistake» means a mistake that was not clever or sensible.
fact: Calling a person stupid is rude, so many people use silly, careless or not a good idea instead.
fact: «Thick as two short planks» is a British joke that means very stupid.
fact: Reading slowly or finding it hard to sit still is not the same as being stupid; many clever people learn differently.
exercise: «It was a stupid mistake to leave the gate open.» What does stupid mean here? | Very quick | Very tall | Kind and gentle | *Not clever or not sensible
exercise: «This stupid zip won't work.» What does stupid describe here? | *Something silly or annoying | Something very kind | Hair | A clever person
exercise: Which word is a kinder choice than calling someone stupid? | Brick-head | Dim-witted fool | Thicko | *Careless
test: «A brick short of a load» is an Australian way of saying what? | Very strong | *Stupid or a bit mad | Fast running | Heavy shopping
test: In a safety talk, «doing something stupid» means what? | *Taking a dangerous risk, like a dare | Finishing a puzzle early | Writing a long story | Being very polite
exam: Why do teachers often ask children not to call a person stupid? | Because it is only used in Australia | Because it means very happy | *Because it is rude and hurts feelings | Because it is a very long word
